Relevant columns / fields and their possible use  
• `event_date`: filter the data to only 20210102 (2‑Jan‑2021).  
• `event_name`: keep only the `'page_view'` rows.  
• `event_params.key / event_params.value.*`  
  – key = `'page_title'`: tells which screen / web page was viewed (e.g. Home, Checkout Confirmation).  
  – key = `'page_location'`: full URL, an alternative way to identify pages.  
  – key = `'ga_session_id'`: the numeric id of the session in GA4.  
• `user_pseudo_id`: combines with `ga_session_id` to make a unique “visit / session” id.  
• `event_timestamp`: lets you sort page views inside a session (not required for the conversion rate itself, but useful for exploration).  

Typical conditions we are going to use  
```
event_date = '20210102'
event_name = 'page_view'
ep.key  = 'page_title'                -- or  'page_location'
LOWER(page_title) LIKE '%home%'       -- get the Home page
LOWER(page_title) LIKE '%checkout%confirmation%'
```

